","description":"","creator":{"login":"gsmet","id":1279749,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzk3NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1279749?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet","html_url":"https://github.com/gsmet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":38,"state":"closed","created_at":"2021-08-30T10:01:13Z","updated_at":"2021-08-31T12:22:49Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2021-08-31T12:22:49Z"},"comments":0,"created_at":"2021-08-27T12:01:56Z","updated_at":"2021-08-30T10:03:35Z","closed_at":"2021-08-28T20:11:41Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nCustom pseudo scope beans are not managed.\r\nThe scope configuration doesn't make the registered scope context class involved in bean lifecycle.\r\n\r\nThe same scope which is registered as a normal works fine.\r\n\r\nThe problem is: normal scope create and uses proxies instead of actual bean classes and this makes impossible to use normal scope in some cases.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nPseudo scope bean is managed, i.e. it's `CustomContext` class is used to create and store a bean instance during the context lifecycle.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n`CustomContext` is never used for pseudo scope.\r\nThe instance is created for every injection point and the context of the scope is disregarded.\r\nAs a result the instance is not reused within the context.\n\n### How to Reproduce?\n\nI have a pseudo scope:\r\n\r\n```\r\n@Scope\r\n@Inherited\r\n@Target({ ANNOTATION_TYPE, TYPE, FIELD, METHOD, CONSTRUCTOR })\r\n@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)\r\npublic @interface CustomScope {\r\n}\r\n```\r\n**Note: It's not a normal.**\r\nI have an  `InjectableContext` implementation class. Let's say it's `CustomContext`.\r\n\r\nI register a `CustomScope` via `@BuildStep`s:\r\n\r\n```\r\n@BuildStep\r\n    ContextConfiguratorBuildItem registerCustomContext(\r\n            ContextRegistrationPhaseBuildItem phase) {\r\n        return new ContextConfiguratorBuildItem(\r\n                phase.getContext().configure(CustomScope.class)\r\n                        .contextClass(CustomScopeContext.class));\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    @BuildStep\r\n    CustomScopeBuildItem customScope() {\r\n        return new CustomScopeBuildItem(CustomScope.class);\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen the `CustomScope` beans are used they are injected but `CustomContext` class methods are never used.\r\nSo neither `CustomContext::get(Contextual)`  nor `Contextual::get(Contextual, CreationalContext)` are ever called.\r\n\r\nThe same scope which is registered as a normal (i.e. with `@NormalScope` and `configure(CustomScope.class).normal()` in the proper places) works fine.\r\n\n\n### Output of `uname -a` or `ver`\n\nDarwin MacBook-Pro 20.6.0 Darwin Kernel Version 20.6.0: Wed Jun 23 00:26:31 PDT 2021; root:xnu-7195.141.2~5/RELEASE_X86_64 x86_64\n\n### Output of `java -version`\n\njava version \"11.0.3\" 2019-04-16 LTS\n\n### GraalVM version (if different from Java)\n\n_No response_\n\n### Quarkus version or git rev\n\n2.0.0.CR3\n\n### Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`)\n\nApache Maven 3.8.2\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"gsmet","id":1279749,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzk3NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1279749?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet","html_url":"https://github.com/gsmet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/19725/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/19725/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}